================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY DATA — NOT COVERED BY THE LICENCE ABOVE AND NOT DISTRIBUTED HERE
================================================================================

This repository contains NO anatomical data. The MIT licence above covers only
the source code written for this project.

At runtime the application can OPTIONALLY download the FreeSurfer `fsaverage`
template surfaces from TemplateFlow. Those files are cached locally in
`neuroforge/_assets/`, which is listed in `.gitignore` and is therefore never
committed or redistributed by this repository. Each user obtains the data
directly from the original source, under that source's own terms.

  fsaverage template surfaces
    Fischl, Sereno, Tootell & Dale (1999). High-resolution intersubject
    averaging and a coordinate system for the cortical surface.
    Human Brain Mapping 8(4):272-284.
    Subject to the FreeSurfer software licence:
    https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/fswiki/FreeSurferSoftwareLicense

  Desikan-Killiany cortical parcellation
    Desikan et al. (2006). An automated labeling system for subdividing the
    human cerebral cortex on MRI scans into gyral based regions of interest.
    NeuroImage 31(3):968-980.

  Distribution
    TemplateFlow — https://www.templateflow.org

If the assets are absent, the application falls back to a fully procedural
cortex generated by this project's own code, which is MIT-licensed like the
rest of the source.

Three.js (rendering, loaded from a CDN at runtime) is MIT-licensed.
